# PROD-03 hygiene — root-level forensic / scratch artifacts produced by
# ad-hoc debugging sessions (analysis scripts, hexdumps, captured worker
# output, local production-like env overrides). They are NEVER part of the
# build: the deployed bundle comes from tracked sources only. Root-anchored
# patterns are deliberate — `_components/`, `__tests__/` and every other
# nested underscore path stays tracked.
/_*.py
/_*.ps1
/_*.bat
/_*.ts
/_*.txt
/_*.log
/_*.json
/.dev.txt
/.dev.err.txt
# Ad-hoc debug scripts under scripts/. Only .ts scratch is covered — the two
# intentionally tracked probe scripts (`scripts/_e2e-token-probe.mjs`,
# `scripts/_probe-factory.mjs`) and every real `scripts/live-*.ts` harness
# stay visible to git.
/scripts/_*.ts

# Local production-like harness overrides (loopback infrastructure). The
# NAMES-only template `.env.production.example` remains tracked; this
# variant must never be committed.
.env.production.localhost-only
# Local scratch: ad-hoc coverage branch analyzer, regenerated per workspace on
# demand. Ignored everywhere (the services/*-only pattern let one get committed
# under packages/knowledge-intelligence).
**/coverage-analyze.mjs

# Mobile (RD-001) — build output & signing material
apps/web/out/
apps/web/android/keystore.properties
apps/web/android/*.jks
.neon
